{"gold": "la", "kind": "term", "sid": "h2-italic-146", "stratum": "italic", "text": "de quinque generibus mirabolanorum", "unit": "2.4.2.3"}
{"gold": "name", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-italic-147", "stratum": "italic", "text": "Muses", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "name", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-italic-148", "stratum": "italic", "text": "Sabellicus", "unit": "3.4.1.2"}
{"gold": "name", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-italic-149", "stratum": "italic", "text": "Chineses", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h2-italic-150", "stratum": "italic", "text": "Si quem conspexerit speciosae formae juvenem, venustate ejus sumitur, & in eum animam intorquet", "unit": "3.2.2.4"}
{"foreign_part": "sine animali", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-001", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Bessonus, and Cardan to this purpose, with many such experiments intimated long since by Roger Bacon in his Tract de Secretis artis & naturae, as to make a chariot to move sine animali", "unit": "2.2.4.1"}
{"foreign_part": "basium nullo fine terminatur, sed semper recens est", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-002", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "always fresh, and ready to begin as at first, basium nullo fine terminatur, sed semper recens est", "unit": "3.2.2.4"}
{"foreign_part": "atque etiam post saevit de futuro", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-003", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "1, atque etiam post saevit de futuro", "unit": "3.4.1.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-004", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "One such a kiss alone, would recover a man if he were a-dying", "unit": "3.2.2.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-005", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "And he, saith Cardan, that leaves his son to a covetous Schoolmaster to be informed, or to a close Abbey to fast and learn wisdom together, doth no other, than that he be a learned fool, or a sickly wise man.", "unit": "1.2.4.2"}
{"foreign_part": "nimia est miseria pulchrum esse hominem nimis", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-006", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "on the other side, Difficile custoditur quod plures amant . And as the bragging soldier vaunted in the Comedy, nimia est miseria pulchrum esse hominem nimis", "unit": "3.3.4.2"}
{"foreign_part": "lucida intervalla", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-007", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "For such men likely have some lucida intervalla", "unit": "1.2.3.12"}
{"foreign_part": "Pullus Jovis", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-008", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Some few amongst the rest, or perhaps one of a thousand, may be Pullus Jovis", "unit": "1.2.3.10"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-009", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Flesh is soft and ruddy, composed of the congealing of blood, &c.", "unit": "1.1.2.3"}
{"foreign_part": "Pythonissae", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "term", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-010", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "lights ever burning as those Vestal virgins, Pythonissae", "unit": "3.4.2.6"}
{"foreign_part": "tanta Corvorum multitudo aedibus morientis insedit, quantam esse in Gallia nemo judicasset", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-011", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "8 telleth such another wonderful story at the death of Johannes de Monteforti a French Lord, Anno 1345, tanta Corvorum multitudo aedibus morientis insedit, quantam esse in Gallia nemo judicasset", "unit": "1.2.1.2"}
{"foreign_part": "omnes omnia bona dicere", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-012", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "All honour, offices, applause, grand titles, and turgent Epithets are put upon him, omnes omnia bona dicere", "unit": "1.2.4.6"}
{"foreign_part": "taedium vitae", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-013", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "a cankered soul macerated with cares and discontents, taedium vitae", "unit": "1.3.1.4"}
{"foreign_part": "nihil aliud nisi imperium spirant", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-014", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "If they do obtain their suit, which with such cost and solicitude they have sought, they are not so freed, their anxiety is anew to begin, for they are never satisfied, nihil aliud nisi imperium spirant", "unit": "1.2.3.11"}
{"foreign_part": "illud angebat", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-015", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "one pulled off his socks, another made ready his bed, a third his supper, all did their utmost endeavours to ease his grief, and exhilarate his person, he was profoundly melancholy, he had lost his son, illud angebat", "unit": "1.3.1.2"}
{"foreign_part": "in secundis", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-016", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "We will not suffer them to be in secundis", "unit": "1.2.3.14"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-017", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "But to the purpose.", "unit": "1.2.1.4"}
{"foreign_part": "lugentes virginitatis florem sic aruisse", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-018", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Better it is indeed to marry than burn, for their souls’ health, but for their present fortunes, by some other means to pacify themselves, and divert the stream of this fiery torrent, to continue as they are, rest satisfied, lugentes virginitatis florem sic aruisse", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"foreign_part": "utinam mihi esset aliquid hic, quo nunc me praecipitem darem", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-019", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "he was weary of his life, sick, mad and desperate, utinam mihi esset aliquid hic, quo nunc me praecipitem darem", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"foreign_part": "caetera sani", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-020", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Of those men I may conclude generally, that howsoever they may seem to be discreet, and men of understanding in other matters, discourse well, laesam habent imaginationem , they are like comets, round in all places but only where they blaze, caetera sani", "unit": "3.4.1.3"}
{"foreign_part": "comes jucundus in via pro vehiculo", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-021", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "and well they deserve it, being that as Magninus holds, a merry companion is better than any music, and as the saying is, comes jucundus in via pro vehiculo", "unit": "2.2.6.4"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-022", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "though their own wives be never so fair, noble, virtuous, honest, wise, able and well-given, they must have change.", "unit": "3.3.1.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-023", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "’Tis an inevitable chance, the first statute in Magna Carta, an everlasting Act of Parliament, all must die.", "unit": "2.3.5.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-024", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "look for Antimony among purgers.", "unit": "2.4.1.4"}
{"foreign_part": "centum puer artium", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-025", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "to have some smattering in all, to be aliquis in omnibus, nullus in singulis , which Plato commends, out of him Lipsius approves and furthers, as fit to be imprinted in all curious wits, not to be a slave of one science, or dwell altogether in one subject, as most do, but to rove abroad, centum puer artium", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-026", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "The Eban stone which Goldsmiths use to sleeken their gold with, borne about or given to drink, hath the same properties or not much unlike.", "unit": "2.4.1.4"}
{"foreign_part": "minus", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-027", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "which Jason Pratensis especially labours, and that they differ only secundum majus or minus", "unit": "1.1.1.4"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-028", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "As Gregory and others inculcate unto us.", "unit": "djr"}
{"foreign_part": "Tempora si fuerint nubila, solus eris", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-029", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "’Tis generally so, Tempora si fuerint nubila, solus eris", "unit": "1.2.4.6"}
{"foreign_part": "animis haec scribo, non auribus", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-030", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "I am aquae potor , drink no wine at all, which so much improves our modern wits, a loose, plain, rude writer, ficum voco ficum, & ligonem ligonem , and as free, as loose, idem calamo quod in mente , I call a spade a spade, animis haec scribo, non auribus", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-031", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Quid nisi pondus iners stolidaeque ferocia mentis", "unit": "2.3.2.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-032", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Quicquid calcaverit hic, Rosa fiet", "unit": "1.2.4.6"}
{"foreign_part": "more aquilae factum", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-033", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "he wondered at the excellency of the shoe and pretty foot, but more aquilae factum", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"foreign_part": "tantum a sapientibus abfuerunt, quantum a viris pueri", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-034", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "As Aelian writ of Protagoras and Gorgias, we may say of them all, tantum a sapientibus abfuerunt, quantum a viris pueri", "unit": "djr"}
{"foreign_part": "Non est volentis nec currentis, sed miserentis Dei", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-035", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "For know this, in conclusion, Non est volentis nec currentis, sed miserentis Dei", "unit": "2.3.3.1"}
{"foreign_part": "factis, natis", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-036", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Many errors and obliquities are on both sides, noble, ignoble, factis, natis", "unit": "2.3.2.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-037", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "are melancholy men for the most part.", "unit": "2.2.2.1"}
{"foreign_part": "circa subtilia Cavillatores pro insanis habuit, palam eos arguens", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-038", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Socrates therefore held all philosophers, cavillers & madmen, circa subtilia Cavillatores pro insanis habuit, palam eos arguens", "unit": "1.2.4.7"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-039", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Accidit hodie terribilis casus", "unit": "1.2.3.13"}
{"gold": "grc", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-040", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Μονὸν ἄργυρον βλέπουσιν", "unit": "3.2.2.3"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "phrase", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-041", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Sed de his satis", "unit": "3.4.1.5"}
{"foreign_part": "primus medicorum", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-042", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "He brags moreover that he was primus medicorum", "unit": "2.4.1.4"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-043", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "This is the safest course, and thou shalt find greatest ease to be quiet.", "unit": "2.3.7.1"}
{"foreign_part": "pauci Promethei, multi Epimethei", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-044", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "pauci Promethei, multi Epimethei . We may peradventure usurp the name, or attribute it to others for favour, as Carolus Sapiens, Philippus Bonus, Lodovicus Pius, &c.", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "name", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-045", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "Roxolana, Suleyman the Magnificent, &c.", "unit": "3.2.2.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-roman-before-bracket-046", "stratum": "roman-before-bracket", "text": "gold and silver are too heavy metals for him to carry that seeks heaven.", "unit": "2.3.3.1"}
