{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-sidenote-049", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "de gest", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"gold": "citation", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-sidenote-050", "stratum": "sidenote", "text": "ibidem", "unit": "2.3.3.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-001", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Aeternitas est illa vox,", "unit": "3.4.2.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-002", "stratum": "verse", "text": "If belly, side and feet be well at ease,", "unit": "2.3.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-003", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Well, Moll, if needs you will be matron-like,", "unit": "2.2.6.4"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-004", "stratum": "verse", "text": "——— quin stultos excutit ignes,", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-005", "stratum": "verse", "text": "No pen could write, no tongue attain to tell,", "unit": "3.3.1.2"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-006", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Lecto te solum, lecto te deprecor uno,", "unit": "3.3.1.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-007", "stratum": "verse", "text": "——— obvius enses", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-008", "stratum": "verse", "text": "My Father’s horse for provender doth stay.", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-009", "stratum": "verse", "text": "So furiously each other did assail,", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-010", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Primum animo tibi proponas quo sanguine creta,", "unit": "3.3.4.2"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-011", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Erat enim induta peplo, igneis radiis splendidiore;", "unit": "3.2.2.3"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-012", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Non sum stultus ut ante jam Neaera,", "unit": "3.2.5.2"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-013", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Vivunt in venerem frondes, omnisque vicissim", "unit": "3.2.1.1"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-014", "stratum": "verse", "text": "——— exigui donum breve temporis,", "unit": "3.2.5.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-015", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Till she or death do make me mute.", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-016", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Their heads, piercing the earth with a fixed eye:", "unit": "1.2.3.15"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-017", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Florente amoris hora,", "unit": "3.2.2.4"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-018", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Having a sting for everyone but me;", "unit": "2.2.6.4"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-019", "stratum": "verse", "text": "I ravish’t am: can the world bring", "unit": "abstract"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-020", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Ne utaris serva, ———", "unit": "3.3.4.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-021", "stratum": "verse", "text": "As raving women turn all topsy-turvy.", "unit": "3.3.2.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-022", "stratum": "verse", "text": "When all are mad, where all are like oppressed,", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-verse-023", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Whatever heavens, sea and land begat,", "unit": "3.4.1.3"}
{"gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-024", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Brachia non hederae, neque vincant oscula conchae.", "unit": "3.2.5.5"}
{"foreign_part": "Sanguine quae vero non rubet, arte rubet", "gold": "la", "kind": "verse", "sid": "h2-verse-025", "stratum": "verse", "text": "Sanguine quae vero non rubet, arte rubet, (Ovid)", "unit": "3.2.2.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-001", "stratum": "english", "text": "Many men have been preferred for their person alone, chosen Kings, as amongst the Indians, Persians, Ethiopians of old;", "unit": "3.2.2.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-002", "stratum": "english", "text": "And so for false fears and all other fortuit inconveniences, mischances, calamities, to resist and prepare ourselves, not to faint is best;", "unit": "2.3.5.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-003", "stratum": "english", "text": "and though her husband did all he could possibly to give her content, in a discontented humour at length she hanged herself.", "unit": "1.2.4.7"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-004", "stratum": "english", "text": "What this humour is, or whence it proceeds, how it is engendered in the body, neither Galen, nor any old Writer hath sufficiently discussed, as Jacchinus thinks: the Neoterics cannot agree.", "unit": "1.1.3.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-005", "stratum": "english", "text": "and howsoever these symptoms be common and incident to all persons, yet they are the more remarkable, frequent, furious and violent in melancholy men.", "unit": "1.3.1.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-006", "stratum": "english", "text": "There are those (saith Bernard) that approve of a mean estate, but on that condition they never want themselves;", "unit": "2.3.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-007", "stratum": "english", "text": "These other may, but are not: and thence come all those headstrong passions, violent perturbations of the Mind;", "unit": "1.1.2.11"}
{"foreign_part": "illa tamen emergens veluti lucida stella cepit elucere, &c.", "gold": "mixed", "kind": "phrase", "mixed_lang": "la", "sid": "h2-english-008", "stratum": "english", "text": "but seeing her by chance, agnovit veteris vestigia flammae , he raved amain, illa tamen emergens veluti lucida stella cepit elucere, &c., she did appear as a blazing star, or an Angel to his sight.", "unit": "3.2.5.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-009", "stratum": "english", "text": "Secondly, for the preservation of the species, and desire of young brood.", "unit": "3.1.1.2"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-010", "stratum": "english", "text": "they are often deceived by the similitude of Symptoms, saith Heurnius, and I could give instance in many Consultations, wherein they have prescribed opposite Physic.", "unit": "2.1.4.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-011", "stratum": "english", "text": "Favorinus urgeth it further, and demonstrates it more evidently, that if a Nurse be misshapen, unchaste, unhonest, impudent, drunk, cruel or the like, the child that sucks upon her breast will be so too;", "unit": "1.2.4.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-012", "stratum": "english", "text": "Hear Fulgentius, God’s invincible goodness cannot be overcome by sin, his infinite mercy cannot be terminated by any: the multitude of his mercy is equivalent to his magnitude.", "unit": "3.4.2.6"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-013", "stratum": "english", "text": "Instead of those accurate Emblems, curious Impresses, gaudy masques, Tilts, Tournaments, &c., they have their Wakes, Whitsun ales, Shepherd’s feasts, meetings on holy-days, country dances, roundelays, writing their names on trees, true lovers’ knots, pretty gifts.", "unit": "3.2.3.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-014", "stratum": "english", "text": "& Cabinet du Roy, their own writer distinctly of the rest;", "unit": "2.3.2.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-015", "stratum": "english", "text": "but such examples are common in Scribonius, Hercules de Saxonia, and others.", "unit": "1.2.1.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-016", "stratum": "english", "text": "and Hannibal’s army by such a panic fear was discomforted at the walls of Rome.", "unit": "1.2.4.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-017", "stratum": "english", "text": "They are so ridiculous and absurd on the one side, so lamentable and tragical on the other;", "unit": "3.4.1.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-018", "stratum": "english", "text": "This likewise should we now have done, had not our will been corrupted;", "unit": "3.4.1.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-019", "stratum": "english", "text": "which because they are impertinent to my purpose, I do voluntarily omit.", "unit": "1.1.2.4"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-020", "stratum": "english", "text": "If in disposition, ill dispositions beget habits, if they persevere, saith Plutarch, habits either are, or turn to diseases.", "unit": "djr"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-021", "stratum": "english", "text": "If more damned than saved, he erroneously concludes, the devil hath the greater sovereignty;", "unit": "3.4.2.6"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-022", "stratum": "english", "text": "will have us to consider well of it, with what kind of Melancholy every one is troubled, for it much avails to know it;", "unit": "1.3.1.3"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-023", "stratum": "english", "text": "Galen the common master of them all, from whose fountain they fetch water, brags lib.", "unit": "2.2.6.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-024", "stratum": "english", "text": "for beauty, dancing, running, leaping, like our silver games.", "unit": "2.2.4.1"}
{"gold": "en", "kind": null, "sid": "h2-english-025", "stratum": "english", "text": "But howsoever this passion of sorrow be violent, bitter, and seizeth familiarly on wise, valiant, discreet men, yet it may surely be withstood, it may be diverted.", "unit": "2.3.5.1"}
